# Telecom Customer Churn Prediction

## Overview
Telecom companies lose 15-25% of customers annually to churn. 
Acquiring a new customer costs 5-10x more than retaining an 
existing one — making early churn prediction a high-value 
business problem.

This project analyses customer-level data from a leading Indian 
telecom firm to predict churn risk among high-value customers 
and identify the key drivers behind switching behaviour.

## Dataset
5,000 customer records across 21 variables including call usage, 
international plans, voicemail, and customer service interactions.

## Approach
- Exploratory data analysis to identify churn patterns
- Feature engineering and outlier detection using IQR method
- Handled class imbalance using SMOTE oversampling
- Built and compared 5 classification models
- Deployed final model as an interactive web app using Streamlit

## Key Findings
- Customers on international plans churned at 42% vs 11% 
  for standard
